---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title={`About Me — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
      description="The personal path behind AlienX, from games and homebrew to networking, self-hosting, and live websites."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="title">
        <p class="eyebrow">ALIENX / ABOUT ME</p>
        <h1 id="title">I learned by making things work.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I was using and changing filesystems before I knew what to call them.
          Games and homebrew led me to networks, self-hosting, and eventually
          websites I could put online.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="journey" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE JOURNEY</p>
        <h2 id="journey-title">One question led to another.</h2>
        <ol class="timeline">
          <li class="timeline-item">
            <span class="number">01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Windows 98 and emulators</h3>
              <p>
                My father introduced me to N64, NES, and SNES emulators on
                Windows 98. The first game I played was Super Mario 64.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="timeline-item">
            <span class="number">02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>A Game Boy of my own</h3>
              <p>
                My own handheld was a Game Boy. I played Zelda without a
                backlight. [Add the Zelda title if you want to name it.]
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="timeline-item">
            <span class="number">03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Homebrew on the Wii and DS</h3>
              <p>
                I used homebrew on a Wii with an HDD and spent a lot of time
                playing Super Mario Galaxy. On the Nintendo DS, I explored SD
                card hacks, played New Super Mario Bros. and other ROMs, and
                even made phone calls through homebrew.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="timeline-item">
            <span class="number">04</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Consoles, phones, and networks</h3>
              <p>
                The PS4 was another stop. [Add what you explored on the PS4.] I
                also explored jailbreaking iPhones. From there I started asking
                how routers, IP addresses, DNS, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and Wi-Fi MAC
                addresses fit together when devices connect.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="timeline-item">
            <span class="number">05</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Home Assistant, Docker, and Unraid</h3>
              <p>
                Home Assistant brought automation into the picture. Docker
                helped me understand how the tools I thought of as apps could
                run as services. Unraid gave me a place to put those services
                together and keep learning how they worked.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="timeline-item">
            <span class="number">06</span>
            <div>
              <h3>VLANs and live websites</h3>
              <p>
                I kept learning the network underneath it all, including VLANs.
                That path now reaches live website deployments, where files,
                services, networks, and an interface all have to work together.
                [Add a launch you want to name.]
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>
      <section class="story" aria-labelledby="story-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE STORY</p>
        <h2 id="story-title">The thread I can see now.</h2>
        <p>
          Back then, I did not have formal words for filesystems or all the
          systems behind a device. I was learning by using files, changing how
          things ran, and following the next question. Homebrew, jailbreaking,
          networking, and self-hosting were different parts of that same habit.
        </p>
        <p>
          I bring that curiosity to websites now. This site is one public
          example: an Astro frontend, Cloudflare hosting, and a release process
          that checks accessibility, browser compatibility, performance, and the
          deployed revision. The homepage shows the production platform and
          systems that can be explored today.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    --about-background: #05070c;
    --about-surface: rgba(18, 23, 36, 0.9);
    --about-surface-alt: rgba(8, 11, 18, 0.9);
    --about-text: #eef2ff;
    --about-heading: #f6f8ff;
    --about-muted: #a5afc3;
    --about-soft: #96a1b7;
    --about-eyebrow: #8f9ab2;
    --about-number: #7f8ba2;
    --about-border: #151b29;
    --about-card-border: #192033;
    --about-accent: var(--brand-green);
    color: var(--about-text);
  }
  main {
    width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 40px));
    max-width: none;
    padding: 5rem 0 8rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--about-eyebrow);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    color: var(--about-heading);
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  h1 {
    max-width: 900px;
    font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 7vw, 6.8rem);
  }
  h1 {
    color: var(--about-heading);
  }
  h1::first-line {
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--about-muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .journey {
    margin-top: 8rem;
    padding-top: 5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--about-border);
  }
  h2 {
    max-width: 850px;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .timeline {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .timeline-item {
    container-type: inline-size;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 72px 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--about-card-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      145deg,
      var(--about-surface),
      var(--about-surface-alt)
    );
    transition:
      border-color 180ms ease,
      transform 180ms ease;
  }
  .timeline-item:hover {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--about-accent) 36%, transparent);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .number {
    color: var(--about-number);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .timeline-item h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }
  .timeline-item p {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    color: var(--about-soft);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  @container (max-width: 420px) {
    .timeline-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
  .story {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-top: 8rem;
    padding-top: 5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--about-border);
  }
  .story p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--about-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
    :global(html:where(:not([data-alienx-theme]))) :global(body) {
      --about-background: #fff;
      --about-surface: #f5f7fb;
      --about-surface-alt: #fff;
      --about-text: #1d2433;
      --about-heading: #0f1219;
      --about-muted: #60739f;
      --about-soft: #687797;
      --about-eyebrow: #64708f;
      --about-number: #687797;
      --about-border: #e1e6ef;
      --about-card-border: #dce2ec;
      --about-accent: var(--brand-green-dark);
    }
    :global(html:where(:not([data-alienx-theme]))) .timeline-item {
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(42, 55, 80, 0.05);
    }
    :global(html:where(:not([data-alienx-theme]))) .timeline-item:hover {
      border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--about-accent) 42%, transparent);
    }
  }
  :global(html[data-alienx-theme='light']) :global(body) {
    --about-background: #fff;
    --about-surface: #f5f7fb;
    --about-surface-alt: #fff;
    --about-text: #1d2433;
    --about-heading: #0f1219;
    --about-muted: #60739f;
    --about-soft: #687797;
    --about-eyebrow: #64708f;
    --about-number: #687797;
    --about-border: #e1e6ef;
    --about-card-border: #dce2ec;
    --about-accent: var(--brand-green-dark);
  }
  :global(html[data-alienx-theme='light']) .timeline-item {
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(42, 55, 80, 0.05);
  }
  :global(html[data-alienx-theme='light']) .timeline-item:hover {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--about-accent) 42%, transparent);
  }
  :global(html:where([data-alienx-theme='light'])) :global(body) {
    --about-background: #fff;
    --about-surface: #f5f7fb;
    --about-surface-alt: #fff;
    --about-text: #1d2433;
    --about-heading: #0f1219;
    --about-muted: #60739f;
    --about-soft: #687797;
    --about-eyebrow: #64708f;
    --about-number: #687797;
    --about-border: #e1e6ef;
    --about-card-border: #dce2ec;
    --about-accent: var(--brand-green-dark);
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    main {
      width: min(100% - 28px, 680px);
      padding-top: 3rem;
    }
    .journey,
    .story {
      margin-top: 5rem;
    }
    .timeline .timeline-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .timeline-item {
      transition: none;
    }
    .timeline-item:hover {
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
